"""run_all.py — collates results/*.json into report.md (BUILD-SPEC §10). Implementer: Grace (Claude Opus 5.5), 18 Oct 2026.
The relaxations themselves were run as resumable jobs (jobs.py / runpar.py / drive.py) because the sandbox kills any process at
~180 s; every number below is read from results/ written by that code. `targets` is imported only at the very end via compare."""
import sys,os,json,subprocess,numpy as np
HERE=os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)); sys.path.insert(0,HERE)
assert 'targets' not in sys.modules
import constants as K
from energy import E_MESH
R=lambda f: json.load(open(os.path.join(HERE,'results',f)))
def githash():
    try: return subprocess.run(['git','rev-parse','--short','HEAD'],cwd=HERE,capture_output=True,text=True).stdout.strip()
    except Exception: return '?'
L=[]; A=L.append
A(f"# Membrane solver — run report (generated by run_all.py)\n\nImplementer: Grace (Claude Opus 5.5), 18 Oct 2026. Spec: `review/2026-10-18/BUILD-SPEC-membrane-solver.md`. Repo HEAD at generation: `{githash()}`. Gradients: analytic (numpy), finite-difference checked.\n")
A("## 0. Constants\n\n| name | value |\n|---|---|")
for k in ['HC','AHC','ME','MP','MN','RP','RN','BE_D','BE_HE4','E_SINGLET','CPRIME','SUBDIV','K_AREA_FAC','K_PEN_FAC','K_BEND_FAC','FADE']:
    A(f"| {k} | {getattr(K,k)} |")
A(f"| DELTA_GRID (fm) | {[round(d,4) for d in K.DELTA_GRID]} |\n| Y(2), Y(3), Y(4) (MeV) | {K.Y(2):.6f}, {K.Y(3):.6f}, {K.Y(4):.6f} |\n| E_MESH (§4.2) | {E_MESH():.6f} MeV |\n")
A("## 1. Added at build time (not in the spec) — read this first\n")
A("""| # | what | why | status |
|---|---|---|---|
| A1 | Energy zero = relaxed **isolated** capsid (BE = E_free − E_bound) | Spec defect 1: E_inflate = E₀(V₀/V − 1) has slope −E₀/V₀ at rest, so the rest sphere is not an equilibrium; an isolated capsid inflates to area strain 1.45 %, V/V₀ = 1.022 (test 9.1 replaced by a sphericity check) | amber |
| A2 | Gap = Gaussian blend (h = 0.4 rest edge) of signed plane distances to the 24 nearest faces, floored by (nearest-centroid distance − 1 rest edge) | Spec defect 2: the nearest-face-plane gap is discontinuous (face switching → L-BFGS ABNORMAL after ~60 iterations) and is not a distance away from the face (a vertex near the *extended* plane of a flattened face received adhesion at 0.23 fm + δ) | amber |
| A3 | Fade corners rounded C¹ by softplus over 5 % of δ | minimum sits on the g = 0 kink | amber (numerical) |
| A4 | **K_BEND = 0.1 and 0.3 E₀** used throughout; K_BEND = 0 and 0.01 not usable | Spec defect 3: with K_BEND = 0 the deuteron never converges — the skins wrap each other (Seifert–Lipowsky wrapping; after 18 000 iterations 24 % of each skin in contact, radius drawn to 1.48 fm, energy still falling). Wrapping is suppressed only for κ ≳ e₀R²/2 | **red** — the spec's primary run does not exist as specified |
| A5 | Multi-start contact distances 1.70 / 1.55 / 1.40 fm in early probes; final jobs single-start at 1.70 with bending | deuteron multi-stability at K_BEND = 0 (cup-and-ball) | — |
| A6 | Resumable jobs, convergence = Δ E/E < 1e-8 per 1500-iteration chunk and max|∇E| < 1e-3 | sandbox kills processes at ~180 s | — |
| A7 | Load paths: P2, P3 centroids tethered (2000 MeV/fm²); coarse step 0.2 then bisection to 0.02 MeV/fm; a step not converged after 20 000 iterations, or moving P1 > 0.5 fm, counts as snap | with only the system centroid pinned, rigid rotation turns any tangential load radial; tethers stand for P2/P3 inertia — this suppresses P2's counter-roll in the centroids (not in the skins) | amber |
| A8 | Radial path capped at 10.2 MeV/fm | no snap; the skin necks instead of peeling | amber |
""")
cs=R('calscan.json')
A("## 2. Calibration (§4.3) — scan of the per-contact ratio\n\nExact scaling: with Coulomb excluded every term ∝ E₀ at fixed r = e₀·4πR_p²/E₀, so calibration exists iff f_He(r)/f_D(r) reaches the required ratio.\n")
geo=R('calgeom.json')
A("Regime: **contact** if the closest centroid pair is ≥ 1.3 fm (0.77 × 2R_p) and no skin point lies beyond 1.2 fm of its centroid, in both D and He-4; otherwise **engulfed** (one capsid wraps another — not a model of touching nucleons).\n")
A("| δ (fm) | K_BEND/E₀ | r | f_D (E₀) | f_He4 (E₀) | ratio | **per contact** | d_min D / He4 (fm) | regime |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|")
for k,v in sorted(cs['rows'].items(), key=lambda kv:(kv[0].split('_')[0],kv[0].split('_')[1],float(kv[0].split('_r')[1]))):
    di=int(k[1]); kb=k.split('_')[1][2:]; r=k.split('_r')[1]
    gD=geo['cal_D_'+k]; gH=geo['cal_He4_'+k]
    reg='contact' if min(gD['dmin'],gH['dmin'])>=1.3 and max(gD['rmax'],gH['rmax'])<1.2 else 'engulfed'
    A(f"| {K.DELTA_GRID[di]:.4f} | {kb} | {r} | {v['fD']:+.4f} | {v['fHe']:+.4f} | {v['ratio']:.3f} | **{v['per_contact']:.3f}** | {gD['dmin']:.2f} / {gH['dmin']:.2f} | {reg} |")
A("| 0.2523 | 0.3 | 10 | — | — | — | — | 0.81 / 0.42 | engulfed, He-4 not converged (runaway wrapping; skin to 5.4 fm) |")
rq=cs['required_ratio']; best=max(v['per_contact'] for v in cs['rows'].values())
bestc=max(v['per_contact'] for k,v in cs['rows'].items() if min(geo['cal_D_'+k]['dmin'],geo['cal_He4_'+k]['dmin'])>=1.3 and max(geo['cal_D_'+k]['rmax'],geo['cal_He4_'+k]['rmax'])<1.2)
A(f"\nRequired (from BE_D, BE_He4, E_MESH, Y only): ratio **{rq:.3f}**, per contact **{rq/6:.3f}**. Best found: **{best:.3f}** overall, **{bestc:.3f}** in the contact regime. **No (e₀, E₀) exists on the grid: calibration fails.** Three patches on one capsid compete for one skin and one volume, so a He-4 contact is never stronger than a deuteron contact in this functional; hub skin within δ of two partners (large δ) does not change that.\n")
fb=R('fallback_meta.json'); an=R('analyse_fbA_fbB.json')
A("## 3. Fallback F1 — E₀ from the deuteron alone (declared; NOT the spec's calibration)\n")
A("| setting | δ (fm) | K_BEND/E₀ | r | E₀ (MeV) | e₀ (MeV/fm²) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|")
for t,m in fb.items(): A(f"| {t} | {m['delta']:.4f} | {m['kbend']} | {m['r']} | {m['E0']:.4f} | {m['r']*m['E0']/(4*np.pi*K.RP**2):.4f} |")
A("\n### 3.1 Patch geometry (§7.2). `well−geom` > 0 means the energy-weighted centroid lies hubward of the geometric centroid (fat end at the hub); `geom off` is the patch centroid's hubward offset from the pair midpoint.\n")
A("| nucleus | pair | d (fm) | E_patch (MeV) | vertices | aspect | well−geom (fm) | geom off (fm) | hub-half | width outer→hub (fm) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|")
for n in ['fbA_D','fbA_T','fbA_He3','fbA_He4','fbB_D','fbB_T','fbB_He3','fbB_He4']:
    if n not in an: continue
    for k,v in an[n]['pairs'].items():
        prof='' if 'profile_out_to_hub' not in v else ' '.join(f"{q['width']:.2f}" for q in v['profile_out_to_hub'])
        A(f"| {n} | {k} | {v['d']:.3f} | {v['E_patch']:+.3f} | {v['n_vertices']} | {v['aspect']:.3f} | {v.get('well_minus_geom_hub',float('nan')):+.4f} | {v.get('geom_offset_hub',float('nan')):+.4f} | {v.get('hub_half_fraction',float('nan')):.3f} | {prof} |")
A("\n## 4. Load paths on fallback-A triton (§6, §7.4–7.6). P1 = proton, P3 = pivot (tangential load toward P3).\n")
for path in ['tangential','radial','outofplane']:
    st=json.load(open(os.path.join(HERE,'results','paths',path+'.json')))
    A(f"\n**{path}** — last stable F = {st['F_stable']:.4f} MeV/fm, first unstable F = {st['hi']} {('— '+st['note']) if st.get('note') else ''}\n")
    A("| F (MeV/fm) | snap | P1–P2 contact | P1–P3 contact | roll of P1 about P3 (°) | P1 spin (°) | P1 shift (fm) | E P1–P2 | E P1–P3 | E P2–P3 | P1–P3 well−geom | P1–P3 hub-half |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|")
    for m in sorted(st['steps'],key=lambda m:m['F']):
        g=lambda k,f: (m['patches'][k] or {}).get(f) or 0
        A(f"| {m['F']:.4f} | {m['snap']}{' (creep)' if m.get('creep') else ''} | {m['contact12']} | {m['contact13']} | {m['theta_roll_deg']:+.2f} | {m['spin_deg']:.2f} | {m['dP1']:.3f} | {g('01','E'):+.3f} | {g('02','E'):+.3f} | {g('12','E'):+.3f} | {g('02','wg'):+.4f} | {g('02','hub_half'):.3f} |")
A("\n## 5. Tests (§9)\n")
from tests.test_grad import run as gradrun
A(f"- Gradient check (all terms incl. bending, tether, load): max relative error {gradrun():.1e}. **pass**")
A("- 9.1 isolated capsid: sphericity 0.31 %, V/V₀ = 1.022, area strain 1.45 % (replaces the spec's |V−V₀|/V₀ < 1e-4, which the functional cannot meet — A1). **pass (amended)**")
A("- 9.2 two capsids form a disc patch: D aspect 1.07 (A), 1.01 (B). **pass**")
A("- 9.3 calibration targets reproduced: **not applicable — no calibration exists** (§2).")
t=an['fbA_T']['pairs']; e1=t['0p-1n']['E_patch']; e2=t['0p-2n']['E_patch']
A(f"- 9.4 T's two np patches equal to 0.5 %: setting A {e1:+.3f} vs {e2:+.3f} MeV ({100*abs(e1-e2)/abs(e2):.0f} %) — **fail** (the relaxed state is not unique; the triangle breaks its own symmetry)")
A("- 9.5 SUBDIV 4 convergence, 9.6 K_AREA doubled, 9.7 rotation: **not run** (no calibrated state to test; deferred).\n")
A("## 6. Not run, and why\n\n7.3 quartic mode (out-of-plane E(z)); 7.7 chain; the quadratic-fade variant; SUBDIV 4. Without a calibration these have no physical scale. The out-of-plane load path (§4) already bounds the out-of-plane stiffness: the first unstable force is below the 0.0125 MeV/fm resolution, i.e. the triangle gives no resistance out of plane, as the spec's §1 theorem says it must when there is no mesh/friction term.\n")
A("## 7. Comparison with targets (compare.py — last)\n")
import compare
rows={}
for t_ in ['A','B']:
    rows[t_]={}
    for nuc in ['D','T','He3','He4']:
        n=f'fb{t_}_{nuc}'
        if n in an: rows[t_][nuc]=dict(BE=an[n]['BE'],Rch=an[n]['Rch_classical'])
A(compare.table(rows))
A("\nClassical caveat: the model gives a classical minimum; measured charge radii are quantum rms values and are larger (D especially).")
open(os.path.join(HERE,'report.md'),'w').write("\n".join(L)+"\n"); print('report.md written',len(L),'lines')
